TinyPixel font adaptation
-------------------------
Copyright videodante 2017. Original: https://videodante.itch.io/tinypixel
Storybound Tiny is a format conversion of TinyPixel from CFF OpenType to
TrueType for Minecraft's font provider. Glyph outlines, character coverage
and advances are preserved. The derivative is renamed to respect the
Reserved Font Name tinypixel and distributed under SIL OFL 1.1.
Conversion script: tools/convert_tinypixel.py.
Full original license: META-INF/licenses/TinyPixel-OFL.txt.
Cyrillic fallback: Storybound Cyrillic, a monochrome bitmap conversion of
Pixelify Sans generated by tools/ExportCyrillicFont.java. The renamed bitmap
derivative is distributed under SIL OFL 1.1; copyright and full license are
bundled in META-INF/licenses/Pixelify-OFL.txt as recorded above.

Field book artwork
------------------
field_book.png is original artwork generated for Storybound using OpenAI
imagegen. The supplied inspiration images were not imported or copied.
Side tabs use the original code-drawn Storybound pixel emblems.

Approved vanilla book artwork (2026-10-25)
-----------------------------------------
vanilla_book.png and vanilla_ribbons.png were generated with the built-in
OpenAI imagegen tool from the original Storybound mockup approved in this
session. No third-party reference pixels were supplied to these edits.
The active journal uses minecraft:default at runtime; no Minecraft font
files are copied into the mod. Resource packs may replace that font.
Earlier straight_book.png and chapter_emblems.png are original generated
prototype assets and are inactive. journal_pixel.png is an inactive
Pixelify Sans bitmap adaptation generated by tools/ExportJournalFont.java,
under the Pixelify OFL notice above.

Journal polish artwork (2026-10-25)
----------------------------------
revised_ribbons.png and traveler_vignette.png are original assets generated
using the built-in OpenAI imagegen tool. The ribbon edit used only the
existing Storybound artwork. No third-party reference images were used.
Only the blue and green regions of revised_ribbons.png are active;
the red and purple bookmarks still use vanilla_ribbons.png.

Page-corner and bookmark revision (2026-10-25)
--------------------------------------------
The previous ribbon atlases are now inactive. BookmarkPixels contains
original code-native 16 by 16 emblems and cloth silhouettes.
traveler_corner.png replaces traveler_vignette.png and was generated using
the built-in OpenAI imagegen tool without external reference images.

Native bookmark icons (2026-10-26)
--------------------------------
BookmarkPixels now renders vanilla Minecraft item icons at runtime.
The earlier custom emblem maps and ribbon atlases are inactive.
No Minecraft icon files are bundled or redistributed in Storybound.

Tonal icon correction (2026-10-26)
---------------------------------
Runtime vanilla bookmark icons were rejected and replaced by original
16 by 16 code-native star, inkwell, crossed swords and skull emblems.
No Minecraft textures or generated images are used for these emblems.

Book material refinement (2026-10-26)
------------------------------------
vanilla_book.png was refined with the built-in OpenAI imagegen tool using
only the existing project texture. The edit reduces uniform dithering and
aligns the top-left brass fitting. No external reference pixels were used.
The edit prompt and provenance are in docs/UI_MATERIAL_REFINEMENT_2026-10-26.md.

Paper dithering (2026-10-26)
---------------------------
The accepted book texture received a paper-only dithering refinement using
the built-in OpenAI imagegen tool and the existing project texture alone.
Prompt and provenance: docs/UI_PAPER_DITHER_2026-10-26.md.
